  client table/individualitemdrop*.xml: one <individualDropBox> per item row). A drop mod is written in the nested
  names; the planner writes a flat row with the flat names below.

  level: 0 = the box (<dropBox>), 1 = the group (<group>), 2 = the item row (<v>). A flat row carries the box and
  group fields of its row.
  convert="bool": nested 1/0, flat True/False.

  <score>: how far the shipped data agrees, per pair of sides (nested side, flat side). A box agrees when the
  multisets of (group, item, value) of the two layouts are equal. common = boxes on both sides; comparable = boxes
  whose rows all carry the field on both sides; agree = boxes that agree; pctAll = agree / common;
  pctComparable = agree / comparable (NA: no comparable box). No boolean conversion and no default is applied in the
  scores, so isApplySmartGenderDrop scores 0 although all 128 comparable boxes agree after 1 = True.

  <unmapped>: nested fields the flat layout has no counterpart for. A flat target gets one summary line per
  mod for them.
-->
